                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "This project examines whether ethnic/racial and gender disparities in child protection decision-making are mediated by stereotypes. Stereotypes are operationalized using the Stereotype Content Model (SCM; perceptions of warmth, morality, and competence). We used an experimental vignette study to examine disparities."
                }
              }
            ]
